Utility interfaces determine conditions at the point of use (@cm-utility-interface: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Cleanroom-Programming-and-Energy-LBNL.lingua#r_36R5RS6HEWBTYN4SHCVPQNP12X", #clean-manufacturing "../../../materials/chemical-feedstocks-and-supply-systems/continuity/Two-suppliers-can-share-the-same-failure.lingua#r_3YJ0DPY2TX68GEYCK057JWJFJX") { r_0K8HB1MA4VJ4RR6G25Q3A66Y1W
**Read:** [Cleanroom programming and energy — Tschudi, Sartor and Xu](../sources/Cleanroom-Programming-and-Energy-LBNL.lingua#r_36R5RS6HEWBTYN4SHCVPQNP12X), process utility planning; revisit [High-purity water is a distribution and measurement problem too](../../../utilities/water-and-sanitation/industrial/High-purity-water-is-a-distribution-and-measurement-problem-too.lingua#r_72TZ7SZVXT1GPW21YQABMTFQSF) and the gas/vacuum and thermal utility Records already connected to this formation.

Water, gas, vacuum, electricity and cooling reach a process through distribution and connection hardware. Conditions at a central plant do not by themselves establish the state at the work point. Demand changes, dead volumes, contact materials, backflow, pressure losses and maintenance intervene.

For each interface, distinguish required quality, quantity, variability, delivery state and recovery after interruption. A utility may serve contamination removal while introducing another contaminant or thermal disturbance.

**Work:** Follow one utility from generation to a sensitive operation and back to a return, drain or waste route. Identify the measurement location and the largest unobserved segment. Compare normal demand, startup and a neighboring process change. Reuse the detailed utility models rather than duplicating their whole subject.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
